{
  "version": 3,
  "why": "N2 + provider limits + N1 under outages: queues split by priority as well as channel (transactional drained by dedicated workers, never behind marketing); a campaign scheduler feeds bulk queues at a controlled rate; per-user frequency caps and per-provider token buckets live in a shared counter store; failed sends go to a delay queue with exponential backoff and finally a dead-letter queue, with idempotency keys preventing duplicates on redelivery.",
